    "scenario": "BGP Attribute AS Path Ignore",
    "goals": "• Configure EBGP between all the ASes.\n  AS {{as1}}: {{router1_name}}\n  AS {{as2}}: {{router2_name}}\n  AS {{as3}}: {{router3_name}}\n  AS {{as4}}: {{router4_name}}\n• Advertise the loopback0 interface on router {{router1_name}} in BGP.\n• Router {{router3_name}} should have two paths to reach network {{router1_loopback0_network}} /{{router1_loopback0_prefix_len}}.\n• Configure AS Path prepending on router {{router2_name}} so router {{router3_name}} sends all traffic to network {{router1_loopback0_network}} /{{router1_loopback0_prefix_len}} through router {{router4_name}}.\n• Configure router {{router3_name}} to ignore AS path length and use BGP router ID as the deterministic tie-break, so it will send traffic for network {{router1_loopback0_network}} /{{router1_loopback0_prefix_len}} to router {{router2_name}}. Don’t use any of the other BGP attributes.",
